From 1c395d090b7120cb4322435184937378225c90d5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pokeheartgold-3ds <bootstrap@invalid>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 05:11:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] gcc: match SDK header signatures to the port sources
 (SDK_PORT_3DS)

Eight header/source mismatches stop the port host32 build with GCC 10
"conflicting types" (s32/u32 are long, a different type from int/void *
even with -m32; MWCC accepts either). Every hunk is guarded by
SDK_PORT_3DS and the DS text is unchanged (identity proof below).

1. lib/include/nitro/mi/memory.h:6 (was: 6-11)
   GCC 10: "conflicting types" for MIi_CpuClear16/Copy16/Clear32/Copy32/
   ClearFast/CopyFast at 3ds_port/nitro/src/mi_memory.c:21,31,53,63,102,107,
   whose parameters are plain void *. Under the macro the six prototypes use
   void * and the header gains the MIi_CpuSend16/Send32 declarations the port
   defines (mi_memory.c:40,71); the DS branch is the original text.
   lib/NitroSDK/include/MI_memory.h already uses void * throughout
   (MIi_CpuSend32 there matches too), so it needs no change.

2. lib/include/nitro/pxi/fifo.h:29 (was: 29-33)
   GCC 10: "conflicting types" for PXI_SetFifoRecvCallback/IsCallbackReady/
   SendWordByFifo at 3ds_port/nitro/src/pxi.c:92,106,119 (int tags vs s32)
   and "unknown type name PXIFifoEmtpyCallback" at pxi.c:113. Under the macro
   the three prototypes use int, and the header gains the EmptpyCallback
   typedef (kept spelling) plus PXI_SetFifoSendCallback with the port's
   single-callback signature. The DS branch is the original text.
   lib/NitroSDK/src/pxi/PXI_fifo.c:61,85,96 (port-replaced) gets the same
   signatures under the macro so the survey parse stays identical.

3. lib/include/nitro/os/cache.h:6 and lib/NitroSDK/include/OS_cache.h:10
   GCC 10: "conflicting types for DC_StoreRange" at
   3ds_port/nitro/src/port_os.c:315, which takes const void *. No other
   DC_*/IC_* in port_os.c differs (register is not part of the type;
   DC_FlushRange already takes const void * in both headers). The DS branch
   is the original line in each file.

4. lib/include/nitro/spi/userInfo.h:26,80
   GCC 10: "NVRAMConfigOwnerInfo has no member named favoriteColor" and
   "NVRAMConfigOption has no member named input_favoriteColor" at
   3ds_port/nitro/src/port_boot.c:46,55. A #define is out:
   lib/include/nitro/os/ownerInfo.h:13 declares OSOwnerInfo.favoriteColor and
   lib/NitroSDK/src/os/os_ownerInfo.c:10 (compiled into the port) touches
   both spellings in one TU, so the macro would rewrite that TU to
   info->favouriteColour, which does not exist. Instead, under the macro each
   whole bitfield run sits in an anonymous union offering both spellings of
   the one differing bit (other members keep a single declaration, so no
   access is ambiguous); wrapping only the one bitfield would split the
   storage unit, so the Option union repeats the full 16-bit run. Layout and
   sizeof are unchanged (OwnerInfo 0x50, Option 0x0c, Data 0x70, Config 0x74).

5. lib/NitroSDK/include/dgt.h:33
   The port (3ds_port/nitro/src/dgt.c:92,120,205,230) defines
   DGT_Hash1SetSource(const void *, unsigned long), DGT_Hash1GetDigest_R
   (void *, ...) and DGT_Hash2SetSource(const unsigned char *, unsigned
   long); the DS u8 * parameters conflict under GCC. Under the macro the
   header uses the port's pointer types (u32 is unsigned long, so the length
   spelling already agrees). lib/NitroSDK/src/math/math_dgt_internal.h:6,
   which redeclares the same six functions, and the port-replaced
   lib/NitroSDK/src/dgt_hash.c:53,90,170 get the same signatures under the
   macro so the survey parse stays identical.

6. lib/include/nitro/card/common.h:120 and lib/NitroSDK/include/CARD_common.h:120
   GCC 10: "'CARDiCommandArg' has no member named 'dst'" at
   3ds_port/nitro/src/port_card.c (ten uses: 254,271,274,278,282,285,288,
   291,297,298), which spells the destination word dst (ntrtwl's name); the
   SDK and the DS game spell it dest. A #define is out for the same reason
   as favouriteColour: CARDiCommon has its own member named dst, used in the
   same translation units (e.g. CARD_rom.c), which the macro would rewrite
   to a nonexistent dest. Instead, under the macro the word sits in
   union { u32 dest; u32 dst; }, so both spellings name offset 16 and
   sizeof(CARDiCommandArg) is unchanged (96 bytes, verified by
   tests/sdk/gcc_fixes). The DS branch is the original line in each file.

7. lib/NitroSDK/src/mi/mi_dma_gxcommand.c:9-15
   GCC 10: "redeclaration of enumerator 'GX_FIFOINTR_COND_*'" and
   "conflicting types for 'GXFifoIntrCond'" once hgss/compat/include is on
   the path: <nitro.h> already brings in GXFifoIntrCond (compat
   nitro/gx/g3x.h) and OS_IE_GXFIFO (compat nitro/os/common/interrupt.h and
   the shared-interrupt wrapper), so the file's local copies collide. Under
   the macro each local copy is skipped when a header already provided it
   (#ifndef OS_IE_GXFIFO, #ifndef HGSS_COMPAT_GX_G3X_H); without
   hgss/compat/include on the path neither guard is defined and the locals
   are still declared here, so standalone SDK builds keep working. The DS
   branch is the original text.

8. lib/NitroSDK/include/dgt.h:20 (struct DGTHash2Context)
   GCC 10: dgt.c's ctx->h0..h4/Nl/Nh/num/data/dummy (dgt.c:151,195-211,230+)
   have no members in the SDK's SAFE/endian-proof struct
   (Intermediate_Hash/Length_Low/...), while MATH_CalcSHA1 (via MATH_dgt.c)
   and the DS game use the HGSS fields. Under the macro the struct body is
   an anonymous union of both layouts, so both spellings compile against the
   one header; each member is 104 bytes, so sizeof(struct DGTHash2Context)
   is unchanged (verified by tests/sdk/gcc_fixes). The DS branch is the
   original struct. The compat header hgss/compat/include/nitro/dgt/dgt.h
   (not part of this patch) now #includes <dgt.h> and typedefs
   DGTHash1Context/DGTHash2Context instead of redefining the structs.

Identity proof (gcc-10 -E -P -m32 -malign-double, the survey defines, CFLAGS
and include order minus -DSDK_PORT_3DS, against the parent commit): the
output is byte-identical for all twelve touched files. With -DSDK_PORT_3DS
eleven differ only in the guarded hunks; mi_dma_gxcommand.c is identical
either way without hgss/compat/include on the path (the guards find nothing
to skip, which is also what keeps standalone SDK builds working).

Checks: tools/sdk_compile_survey.py --m32 --gcc gcc-10: 269/284 before and
after (same 15-file failing set; warnings unchanged at 563).
tools/port_compile_survey.py: 45/46 before (only port_card.c: dst), 46/46
after. python3 tools/hgss_nitro.py make --target host32 --out <dir> lib -k:
exit 0, 0 error lines, libnitro.a produced (dgt.o, port_card.o,
CARD_common.o and mi_dma_gxcommand.o all build).
tests/sdk/gcc_fixes/run.sh: all 11 groups pass (7 new); on the previous
1202 revision the 2 new positive checks fail the way the port build did
(no member named 'dst' / 'h0') while (a)-(i) still pass.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
